# A ConfigMap mounted as a directory is not a plain directory. Kubernetes
# writes the real files into a timestamped folder and leaves behind symlinks:
#
#   /opt/airflow/dags/
#     ..2026_08_12_12_07_22.1352022888/   <- real files
#     ..data -> ..2026_08_12_12_07_22.1352022888
#     ingest_qlgia.py -> ..data/ingest_qlgia.py
#
# Airflow walks the DAG folder with followlinks=True, meets the timestamped
# folder twice — once directly, once through ..data — and refuses to continue:
#
#   RuntimeError: Detected recursive loop when walking DAG directory
#
# Pruning both entries avoids it. The ignore filter runs before the recursion
# check in airflow._shared.module_loading.file_discovery, so this is enough.
#
# Syntax is glob (core.dag_ignore_file_syntax), which uses gitignore matching:
# a pattern with no slash matches by name at any depth.
..*
